<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Hardened-runtime entitlements for the notarized Audio Cleaner.app. Kept minimal on purpose.

    Needed by this bundle:
      com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
        Under the hardened runtime the app may only load libraries signed by Apple or by the same team. CI
        re-signs every Mach-O file in the bundle with our identity, so the shipped app would run without this
        entitlement. It is kept because the LGPL requires users to be able to replace Qt (and FFmpeg, libdf)
        with their own builds: a replaced, differently signed Qt library would otherwise be refused and the
        app would not start. If you decide that replaceability on macOS is not needed, delete the key
        and test a notarized build.

    Deliberately NOT included:
      com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory, allow-dyld-environment-variables
        Python, NumPy, CTranslate2 and ONNX Runtime run without a JIT. Add them only if the frozen app crashes
        on a notarized build with a code-signing / memory-protection error in the crash log.
      com.apple.security.app-sandbox
        The app reads and writes files the user picks anywhere on disk and starts ffmpeg as a child program;
        it is distributed outside the Mac App Store, where the sandbox is optional.
      Audio input / camera
        The app only processes files; it never records.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
